  "reason": "The best result so far is config_027 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.7062). The key remaining uncertainty is whether transformer aggregation could outperform avgpool when paired with the richer, nonlinear scvi_n200 embeddings. With pca_n2000, transformer was notably worse (0.5856 vs 0.6352), but PCA produces linear projections that may not benefit from attention-based token weighting, whereas scvi_n200 yields learned latent representations where attention could selectively emphasize informative dimensions. This experiment tests that hypothesis directly. If transformer helps, it could push accuracy above 0.7062; if not, it confirms avgpool as optimal and frees the remaining 3 experiments to exploit the confirmed best architecture with other variations (e.g., fusion strategy via config_020, or singleprofile settings). This is the highest-information experiment that extends the strongest finding."
